  "contract": [
    "Scan up to eight24-byte headers, reusing initialized scratch; a free slot requires both word8 and word12 equal FFFFFFFF. Other padding/header bytes retain the most recent read.",
    "Snapshot initial header base and compute next payload from occupied header length/offset and live partition base. Reload device callbacks at each read/write boundary.",
    "Aligned length=(length+3)&FFFC, including 16-bit wrap. Compare unsigned wrapped payload end against live sector end; overflow requests finalize but returns0.",
    "Write aligned payload first; only zero status succeeds. Then read live input fields10/12/16, compute actual Modbus CRC over aligned bytes and program exactly20 header bytes.",
    "On success log original length and slot+1; return1 except slot7 returns the full finalizer result. Nonzero payload/header status logs failure and returns0.",
    "Caller must provide valid source extent of at least max(20,aligned length), and valid live partition/device providers. No new capacity or null contract is inferred."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Direct FAL and finalize/logging boundaries modeled; actual C CRC16/EABI clear/memset execute. Guarded source execution cannot enter stock.",
    "Parent fixture executes retained record-store assembly, C sector write, CRC and erase/count core; selection, finalize, FAL and logging modeled.",
    "Preserved native 16-bit length wrap, unsigned address arithmetic, failed/partial-read scratch carry and zero-only write-success rule are compatibility evidence, not physical reliability proof.",
    "Saved integer/FP registers, masks, caller-stack and input guards checked. Private frames, APSR, incidental void provider returns, concurrency/faults excluded.",
    "Physical NOR programming, finalization service, power-loss behavior, final application linking and boot remain unverified."
  ],
